    "body": "Hi, and thanks for the quick reply on #8075.\n\nThe patch and the description below were prepared with Claude (Claude Code). I went through them before submitting and will handle the review myself.\n\nFixes #8075\n\nCPython 3.13+ dedents docstrings at compile time (gh-81283). This makes Cython do the same, following `_PyCompile_CleanDoc()` (which differs from `inspect.cleandoc()`).\n\n`help()` and `inspect.getdoc()` clean docstrings anyway, but code that uses the raw `__doc__` doesn't. We noticed this because LangChain's `@tool` sends `__doc__` to the LLM as the tool description, so compiling a module changed that text. The same applies to anything that prints or compares `__doc__`, e.g. argparse with `RawDescriptionHelpFormatter`.\n\nAs discussed in the issue, this applies regardless of the Python version, with no directive and no `language_level` restriction. Verbatim C code in `cdef extern from *:` blocks is left as is, since dedenting could change string literals.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
