                "message": "Dedent docstrings at compile time like CPython 3.13\n\nSince Python 3.13 (gh-81283), the CPython compiler strips the common\nindentation from docstrings.  Cython kept it, so compiled modules\nexposed a different __doc__ than CPython 3.13+.\n\nApply the same cleanup as _PyCompile_CleanDoc() when docstrings are\nparsed, regardless of the Python version at runtime.  The verbatim C\ncode in 'cdef extern from' blocks is left untouched.\n\nFixes #8075\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "524c2636334561dad59b7a65df7bc3cbb2868778",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/trees/524c2636334561dad59b7a65df7bc3cbb2868778"
